 # voidc command reference
+
+Slice 1 adds an explicit compiler-library parser only. It introduces no command,
+option or automatic manifest lookup; the future forms below still reject in current
+voidc. [Qualification](projects/SLICE1.md) includes malformed manifests beside ordinary
+source, unchanged directory/main.void selection, explicit JIT/AOT and absent zero-ID
+OS calls. Later project-command integration remains deferred.
+
+The [Phase 1 command/compatibility proposal](PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE_ROADMAP.md#phase-1-ownership-and-data-flow)
+freezes `--project DIR`, manifest-relative `--entry PATH` and `--profile debug|release`
+as future project options. A selected manifest enables new discovery; bare explicit
+files and manifestless directories retain current semantics. Project default profile
+is release/O2, and conflicting explicit profile/cache choices diagnose. Proposed
+examples only, **not executable baseline commands**:
+
+```text
+voidc check --project .
+voidc run --project . -- literal-application-argument
+voidc build --project . --entry src/launcher.void --profile debug
+voidc init . --name Orbit --app-id org.example.orbit
+voidc new orbit --source src/game.void --app-id org.example.orbit
+```
+
+The [creation contract](PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE_ROADMAP.md#proposed-first-file-creation-and-terminal-workflows)
+creates no dependency installation authority, never overwrites manifests or renames
+sources, and omits entry by default. Detailed options remain proposed pending review.
+Implementation is HOLD.
 
